:"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":27,"endLine":11,"startColumn":20,"startLine":11}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `#secret` is a private class member name, which only code inside its class can use\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** use a public property name: `.secret`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `#secret` is a private class member name, which only code inside its class can use"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":409,"start":402},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":27,"endLine":11,"startColumn":18,"startLine":11}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":20,"endLine":12,"startColumn":18,"startLine":12}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: the value is only a comment, not an expression\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** an `expr` must produce a value: write the expression, or move the comment into a `<script>` or an XML comment `<!-- … -->`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: the value is only a comment, not an expression"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":432,"start":430},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":36,"endLine":12,"startColumn":18,"startLine":12}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":19,"endLine":13,"startColumn":18,"startLine":13}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: unterminated template literal\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** close the template literal with a matching backtick; to include a backtick inside it, escape it with `\\`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: unterminated template literal"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":470,"start":469},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":13,"startColumn":18,"startLine":13}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":502,"endColumn":10,"endLine":15,"startColumn":9,"startLine":15},"insertedContent":{"text":"//"}}]}],"description":{"text":"start the comment with `//`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":10,"endLine":15,"startColumn":9,"startLine":15}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `<script>`: `#` does not start a comment in ECMAScript\n\n**Note:** a script that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and aborts the rest of its executable-content block\n\n**Help:** write the comment with `//` (a Markdown heading does not belong in a script)\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `<script>`: `#` does not start a comment in ECMAScript"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":503,"start":502},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `<script>`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-lexer-wording.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":7,"endLine":17,"startColumn":15,"startLine":14}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.9.4: \"The SCXML Processor MAY reject documents containing syntactically ill-formed expressions at document load time, or it MAY wait and place 'error.execution' in the internal event queue at runtime when the expressions are evaluated.\" This toolchain takes the second option, so the document compiles and the expression raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated (a condition is then false and the rest of an executable-content block is skipped); this check runs only when the host supplies the data model's parse-only syntax capability (the native CLI links the ECMAScript and XPath checkers). Each finding names the offending source text and, where a repair is certain to parse, offers it: ECMAScript habits in XPath (`==` to `=`, `&&` to `and`, `||` to `or`, `!x` to `not(x)`, `length()` to `string-length()`), a stray `=` in ECMAScript (`x === = 3`), word operators, quoting, and more. The XPath data model has no script language, so a non-empty `<script>` is reported too"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: apply the suggested repair, or fix the syntax at the marked position following the finding's help; for XPath, use XPath 1.0 operators and functions (`=`, `and`, `or`, `not()`, `string-length()`, `count()`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML038` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ecma-profile","id":"SCXML038","name":"SCXML038","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression or script does not parse in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}